{
  "id": "Compound::DB00932 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Tipranavir is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2d6 through a series of molecular interactions involving Cyp2c19. The evidence suggests that Tipranavir binds to Cyp2c19, which in turn is bound by either Proguanil or Moclobemide, both of which are known to interact with Cyp2d6. This creates a chain of enzymatic and pharmacological relationships, where Tipranavir indirectly influences Cyp2d6 through its interaction with Cyp2c19 and the subsequent binding of other compounds to this enzyme. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Tipranavir to Cyp2d6 highlights the potential for Tipranavir to modulate Cyp2d6 activity via a complex network of enzyme interactions. The integration of these pathways underscores the role of Cyp2c19 as a critical mediator in the pharmacological effects of Tipranavir on Cyp2d6, emphasizing the importance of enzyme-bound compounds in drug-target interactions.",
